# RaktSetu — two environment variables, one of which is a secret.
#
# THE DATA LAYER
#
# In PRODUCTION the authoritative database is a REMOTE libSQL/Turso database,
# reached over HTTPS. That is what makes a genuinely $0 deployment possible: a
# free host has no persistent disk, so the data lives in a hosted database
# instead of in a file beside the application.
#
# In LOCAL DEVELOPMENT neither variable is set, and the app uses a local SQLite
# file under ./data via Node's built-in `node:sqlite`. That is correct and
# complete for development and for the test suite; it is NOT the production
# arrangement.
#
# RAKTSETU_DATABASE_URL
#   The remote database URL, e.g. libsql://your-db.turso.io
#   Unset, the local file backend is used.
#
# RAKTSETU_DATABASE_TOKEN
#   The server-only auth token for that database. Treat it as a password: it is
#   read only in src/lib/server/driver.ts, is never exposed to the browser, and
#   is never written to a file that is committed to git. Set it in your host's
#   secret store (see README).
#
# RAKTSETU_DATA_DIR
#   Only used by the LOCAL file backend — the directory holding raktsetu.db.
#   Unset, it defaults to ./data. It is ignored in production.
#
# `npm run check:invariants` enforces that ONLY src/lib/server/db.ts and
# src/lib/server/driver.ts read process.env, that no NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable is
# read anywhere, and that no client component imports a storage module.

